course: dictionary
lesson: 13200
title: Fumes: smoke, smell and anger
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fumes is a noun. It is gas or smoke that smells strong and can be harmful to breathe. «The paint fumes made the room hard to breathe in.» The clues are paint and hard to breathe in, so fumes must be something in the air that you breathe.
explain: The same family of words can also be a verb. Fume, fumes, fumed and fuming mean to be very angry, often quietly. «Dad was fuming in the car after the traffic jam.» Here fuming does not mean smoke. The clue is the feeling: Dad is cross and keeping it in.
explain: To tell which meaning is right, ask: is this a thing you can breathe, or a feeling someone has? Then swap in your meaning and check the sentence still makes sense. «Open the window before you use the glue» fits the gas meaning. «Mum fumed when the bus was late» fits the anger meaning.
explain: Fumes often appear in safety lessons. Car exhaust fumes, petrol fumes and toxic fumes can make you dizzy or ill. Use things outside or in a well-aired room, never mix cleaning products, and tell an adult straight away if you feel unwell.
fact: Fumes (noun) means gas or smoke that smells strong and can be harmful to breathe.
fact: Fume (verb) means to be very angry, often quietly, as in «fuming with anger».
fact: Fumes come from car exhausts, petrol, paint, glue, cleaning products and fires.
fact: Toxic fumes can make you dizzy or ill, so get fresh air and tell an adult.
fact: In science, burning fuels gives off fumes that pollute the air.
exercise: «The paint fumes made the room hard to breathe in.» What are fumes in this sentence? | A bright, sunny colour | *Gas or smoke that smells strong and can harm you | A loud noise from the street | A kind of paint brush
exercise: «Dad was fuming in the car after the traffic jam.» What does fuming mean? | Driving very fast | *Very angry, often quietly | Coughing and sneezing | Laughing loudly
exercise: Why should you open a window when you use glue or paint? | To make the room colder for fun | To let in the sound of birds | *To let the fumes out so the air is safer to breathe | To stop the paint from drying
test: «Car exhaust fumes can make you dizzy, so stay away from them.» What can fumes do to you? | *Make you dizzy or ill | Make your hair curl | Make you hungry for cake | Make you taller
test: Which word means very angry in «Ben fumed when the rain spoiled his picnic»? | *fumed | picnic | spoiled | rain
exam: Which sentence uses fumes to mean gas or smoke? | He fumes every time it rains. | She fumed about the late bus all morning. | *Toxic fumes came from the spilled chemicals.
